<!-- Droids are machines: they break and are REPAIRED, never tended.

     THE PROBLEM, measured against the live dump 2026-08-11.

     Verse.RaceProperties resolves this way (decompiled, do not re-derive):

         public bool IsMechanoid => FleshType == FleshTypeDefOf.Mechanoid;
         public bool IsFlesh     => FleshType.isOrganic;

     So EMP and ion stun key off the FLESH TYPE'S isOrganic flag, not off the
     def being named "Mechanoid". Of the 57 droid races installed:

         fleshType                       isOrganic   defs   ion works?
         Mechanoid          (JDS)          False      16       yes
         Asimov_Automaton   (Outer Rim)    TRUE       19       NO
         ABF_..._Synstruct  (KotOR)        TRUE       22       NO

     41 of 57 droids were ORGANIC to the engine. Ion and EMP did nothing to
     them, colonists could bandage them, and the Jawa signature weapon was
     useless against the enemy it exists to fight. This inverts L4 (ion
     disrupts), L5 (stun mirrors ion) and L16 (lightning is the neural verb)
     for 72% of the droid roster.

     WHY THIS IS A TWO LINE FIX AND NOT A 41 DEF ONE.

     Both frameworks already declare their droids as machines in every other
     respect: Damage_HitMechanoid effecter, mechanoid wound textures, and (for
     Synstructs) CorpsesMechanoid as the corpse category. Only isOrganic
     disagrees with the rest of each def. Patching the two FleshTypeDefs fixes
     every race that uses them, now and for any the mods add later, and leaves
     each mod's own wound art and corpse handling untouched.

     Retargeting 41 race defs to vanilla Mechanoid would have thrown that art
     away and broken on the next mod update. One flag is the smaller claim.

     WHAT TO WATCH after this lands (all intended, but verify in play):
       * colonists can no longer TEND droid injuries; repair is the route
       * EMP, ion and stun now land on Outer Rim and KotOR droids
       * droids stop registering as organic for anything that checks IsFlesh

     Authorised by the project owner 2026-08-11: "I don't want to be able to
     medically TEND droids anyway. They should break like machines, and get
     repaired."

     WRITTEN BY HAND, not by a generator. This is a doctrine ruling rather than
     a computed value, so it does not belong in Jawa_Armoury. -->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods><li>Asimov</li></mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <!-- 19 Outer Rim Droid Depot races: GNK, MSE, DUM, R series, FX-7,
           Astromech, Protocol, Battle, Commando, MagnaGuard, Destroyer, HK,
           KX Security, Imperial Labor, Salvage Assist and the rest. -->
      <xpath>/Defs/FleshTypeDef[defName="Asimov_Automaton"]/isOrganic</xpath>
      <value><isOrganic>false</isOrganic></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods><li>ABF: Synstructs Core</li></mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <!-- 22 KotOR droid races: 3C series, AD Mk I and Mk IV, Dev AD and WD,
           GE3LD, HK series, war droids and their Sith variants. -->
      <xpath>/Defs/FleshTypeDef[defName="ABF_FleshType_Synstruct_Base"]/isOrganic</xpath>
      <value><isOrganic>false</isOrganic></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
